{/eq}
To find the limit, we can simplify the function first:

{eq}\begin{align*}

\displaystyle \lim_{x \rightarrow 0} \frac {\cot 3x}{4 \csc 2x}

& =\displaystyle \lim_{x \rightarrow 0} \frac {\frac{\cos3x}{\sin3x}}{\frac{4}{\sin2x}} \\

& =\displaystyle \lim_{x \rightarrow 0}  \frac{\cos3x}{\sin3x} \cdot \frac{ \sin2x}{ 4} \\

& =\displaystyle \lim_{x \rightarrow  0 } \frac{\cos3x}{4} \cdot \frac{\sin2x}{\sin3x}  \\

& =  \displaystyle \frac{\cos3(0)}{4} \cdot \frac{\sin2(0)}{\sin3(0)} \\

& =  \displaystyle \frac{\cos0}{4} \cdot \frac{\sin0}{\sin0} \\

& =  \displaystyle \frac{1}{4} \cdot \frac{0}{0} \\

\end{align*}

{/eq}

Since we have an indeterminate form, we can use L'Hopital's Rule to evaluate the limit:

{eq}\begin{align*}

\displaystyle \lim_{x \rightarrow 0} \frac {\cot 3x}{4 \csc 2x}

& =\displaystyle \lim_{x \rightarrow \infty}  \frac{\cos3x}{4} \cdot \frac{\sin2x}{\sin3x}  \\

& =  \displaystyle \lim_{x \rightarrow 0 }  \displaystyle  \frac{\cos3x}{4} \cdot \left [ \lim_{x \rightarrow 0}  \displaystyle \frac{\sin2x}{\sin3x}  \right ] \\

& =   \displaystyle  \frac{1}{4} \cdot \left [ \lim_{x \rightarrow 0}  \displaystyle \frac{2\cos 2x }{3 \cos 3x}  \right ]  &\textrm{[Use L'Hopital's Rule]}\\

& =   \displaystyle  \frac{1}{4} \cdot \left [ \displaystyle  \frac{2\cos 2(0) }{3 \cos 3(0)}  \right ]\\

